    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and it passes. The full build succeeds.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the welcome-notification side-effect for successful owner creation.\n\n**New component** \u2014 `WelcomeNotifier` (`rest/controller/WelcomeNotifier.java`): a small, single-responsibility Spring `@Component` that emits one line via the `NOTIFY` logger containing the owner id and member id. I kept this separate from the existing `OwnerCreationAuditLogger` (which logs to the `AUDIT` logger) rather than overloading that class, so each notifier owns exactly one channel.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`: injected `WelcomeNotifier` via the constructor (matching the existing DI pattern) and called `welcomeNotifier.enqueueWelcome(owner)` right after the owner is saved and audited, so the id and member id are populated. This is on the sole success path (after all validation/duplicate/quota short-circuits), so it fires only on a successful create.\n\n**Verification** \u2014 the acceptance test `coreEnqueuesWelcome` passes, and the full `./mvnw test` build is green. The captured log confirms the behavior:\n```\nINFO  NOTIFY - Welcome notification enqueued: id=11 memberId=NSW2616E6609E3\n```",
